    "answer": {
      "short": "The Kookaburras’ percentage stayed at $75\\%$, because their latest game's goals-for to goals-against ratio, $15:20$, equals their previous ratio, $90:120$.",
      "worked": "For the Kookaburras:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Old percentage}&=\\frac{90}{120}\\times100\\%\\\\\\text{Old percentage}&=75\\%\\\\\\text{New percentage}&=\\frac{90+15}{120+20}\\times100\\%\\\\\\text{New percentage}&=\\frac{105}{140}\\times100\\%\\\\\\text{New percentage}&=75\\%\\end{align*}$$\nTheir old ratio $90:120$ and their latest game's ratio $15:20$ both simplify to $3:4$. Adding goals in the same ratio leaves the percentage unchanged. The other seven teams’ percentages change.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
